# Store

- One SQLite database (`modernc.org/sqlite`) per data directory, opened by `store.Open` with WAL, `busy_timeout=5000`, foreign keys and `_txlock=immediate` (transactions take the write lock at BEGIN, so invariant checks inside `withTx` are race-free).
- Schema changes are new files `migrations/NNNN_description.sql`, applied in order, each in its own transaction together with its `schema_migrations` row. Never edit an applied (shipped) migration. A database newer than the binary is refused.
- Each resource id is `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`: ids are never reused (sessions, job logs, subjects and checkouts are keyed by them). `accounts.token_version` is random per row and bumped with `nextTokenVersion`.
- Timestamps are TEXT in the fixed-width layout `2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z` (lexically sortable); use `formatTime` and `parseTime`.
- Methods return domain structs and the sentinels `ErrNotFound`, `ErrConflict` (UNIQUE violation), `ErrMissingReference` (foreign key, e.g. a server's build deleted meanwhile), `ErrLastAdmin`, `ErrSelf` and `ErrLimit` (quota, e.g. API tokens); HTTP mapping belongs to the caller. Keep SQL parameterised; check-then-insert quotas run inside `withTx`.
- The database file is pre-created 0600 by `datadir.Prepare` so `-wal`/`-shm` inherit the mode.
- Encrypted columns (`projects.auth_secret`, `servers.env`, `servers.admin_token`) are opaque `[]byte` here. `CreateProject` and `CreateServer` take a `SealFunc` that is called with the new id inside the insert transaction, so ciphertext can be bound to the row (`CreateServers`, the all-or-nothing batch used by import, takes one per index). Fields holding secrets or hashes are tagged `json:"-"`.
- Builds (`builds.go`): `ReconcileBuilds` runs at startup with `Reconcile`; deletions that must respect references go through `DeleteBuildUnused` / `DeleteProjectUnused` (one transaction; `ErrActive`, `ErrInUse`). Successful build deletions enqueue image cleanup in the same transaction. `RecordBuildExport` persists ownership before Docker runs; a successful finish atomically clears that export intent. Project build maintenance pages by id. `projects.static_addons` is a JSON array read into `Project.StaticAddons` (never nil) and written only by `UpdateProjectRemote`.
- `Reconcile` runs once at startup: active jobs become `error` "interrupted by daemon restart" and transient project statuses (`cloning`, `pulling`, `switching_branch`) become `error`. Update its status list when adding transient statuses. Project jobs and PATCH write disjoint columns (`SetProjectCheckout`, `UpdateProjectRemote`) so they cannot overwrite each other; likewise server jobs (`SetServerDesiredState` and launch/container operations, which also own `admin_token`) and PATCH (`UpdateServer` with a `ServerUpdate`: build, port, allowed origins, env compare-and-swapped, `ErrStale` on a lost race). Servers reference builds (`servers.build_id`, a build in use cannot be deleted). `UpdateServer` enforces same-project successful builds and checks for queued or running server jobs in its write transaction. It also rejects a port write based on a superseded container ID. `LatestSuccessfulBuild` and `BuildsByImage` serve import and the image views.
- Migration versions may have gaps (0005 was reserved and is unused; 0007 adds the builds' transport paths, 0008 launch recovery state, 0009 build hardening). Tests compare against the embedded migration list, not the highest version.
- Typed settings (`GetSettings`/`UpdateSettings`) include `game_host` (validated by callers with `certs.ValidateHost`); the certificate mode key `game_certificate_mode` is owned by `internal/certs` and commits the staged certificate generation as well as the mode. Certificate commits and launch identities use a fully synced write before publishing files or starting Docker operations.
- `InstanceID` creates the installation's random instance id once (settings key `instance_id`, never returned by the API); Docker objects are labelled with it.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/store/...`.
